This is my first wishless/arch/dwarf ascension, but most importantly
this is my first with ASCII graphics. My first 4 were with tiles as
that is how I was introduced to nethack. After my monk I got to reading
some debates on whether ASCII or tiles were superior. It got me
interested as to why people favoured ASCII so much.

So I decided one day to try it. Man, I felt like a fish out of water. I
think the thing that was really bugging me is all the black. I got used
to it and started discovering what all the symbols meant.
The more I played more I realized that it wasnt that different after
all. I was worried that I would constantly be using farsight to see
what things were, but I found that after a while I rarely had to use
it. After just 1 ascention (and one that died a YASD at orcus's town) I
was just as comfortable playing with ASCII than with tiles. And I ain't
going back ;)

If you are used to using tiles id recommend you try it for a day or two
at least and see if you like it.


Onto my Arch's game.

I dont feel like writing a big long post so I'll sum up the important
parts

I began the game with a protection run. The minetown temple was chaotic
and Izchak had a nice magic lamp in stock. This was a wishless game so
I had a good lightsource most of the game. I then headed down to
sokoban where a "oR (I can now understand all the abbreviations using
symbols =3DD) was waiting for me. I went back to the mines to get me
lucky charm but I found one early on teh level below the minetown. I
decided to continue anyways to get goods. One of the levels I found a
BoH.

After that I dwelved further down the dungeons in search of altars.
Instead I found a throne that let me genocide mind flayers. I found an
altar that I converted quickly and got myself some holy water and made
a junk-item stash. I had 2 b?oG which got ride of ; and L. I found the
quest portal and medusa's lair. I wanted MR before going any further so
I did the quest. I didnt have any form of levitation yet but 2 scrolls
of earth got me and my 8 baby silver dragons across the water. Killed
medusa and stormed the castle. I lost 3 dragons in the storming. Wand
was 0:3 (rng is a tease). I used a !oL to get to the item stashes and
was rewarded with levitation boots. In VotD the rest of my dragons were
wiped out. None got to fully grow, though I had them since I made my
junk item stash a while back. Though I was happy again when I found a
=3DoL there.

I was overflowing with useless crap so I made my way back to my item
stash and did some polypiling. I got [GoP and [HoB and many good
potions/scrolls.

My weapon was a silver sabre through most of this. I didnt feel like
wasting alot of time trying to get grayswandir. I got me through hell
pretty good. I didnt come across and magic markers or many ?oEW so I
only got it to a max of  +4 (knocked to 0 after being frustrated with a
disenchanter).

I didnt encounter much trouble in hell. Though I did waste about 5000
turns trying to find the stairs to Vlad. Turned out it was in a tiny
hallway I didnt completely investigate. Rawr.

The middle tower section was pretty fun. A cockatrice was in the
hallway just before the big monster filled room and it left a corpse.
*whack* "turns to stone" *whack* "turns to stone" *whack* "turns to
stone" *whack* "turns to stone". Good times.

Killed rodney, c?oT to the bottom level and got the amulet easily. Then
came the part I hate most about lawfuls. I must have been sent down a
total of about 30 times. Argh!

>From the castle to the astral plane I didnt have any trouble. I only
had 3 ?oGD so I did the plane of earth manually, but I found the portal
pretty fast. Astral plane was a b*tch, I tell ya. With just a +0 silver
sabre as a weapon it was pointless to fight anything but the summoned
insects. Lucky I was overflowing with /oT. I go to the center, famine,
not my altar. I go right, pesty, not my altar. I had to go through
death, worst case scenario. With my weapon it would take forever to
take him down and I had abandoned my daggers since I couldnt enchant
them. I lured him to the middle room where famine was luckly way up
around the altar and danced around the priests/angels and made my way
back with him on my tail. I got to the altar and the rest is history. 8
roles, 3 races and 4 conducts to go.


